{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-66263","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-98355","text":"Graphonomous FAQ"}]},{"id":"blk-66264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98356","text":"This page answers the most common questions about Graphonomous, its MCP interface, and operating model."}]},{"id":"blk-66265","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-98357","text":"What is Graphonomous?"}]},{"id":"blk-66266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98358","text":"Graphonomous is a continual-learning memory engine for AI agents. It stores knowledge as a graph, supports confidence-updating feedback loops, and exposes all capabilities through MCP tools/resources."}]},{"id":"blk-66267","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-98359","text":"Does Graphonomous retrain model weights?"}]},{"id":"blk-66268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98360","text":"No. Graphonomous does "},{"id":"spn-98361","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-98362","text":" retrain model weights. Learning happens in the memory graph by storing knowledge and updating confidence based on outcomes."}]},{"id":"blk-66269","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-98363","text":"What problem does it solve?"}]},{"id":"blk-66270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98364","text":"It gives agents durable, evolving memory and better decision quality over time by combining:"}]},{"id":"blk-66271","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-66273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98365","text":"semantic retrieval"}]}],"id":"blk-66272","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-66275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98366","text":"graph neighborhood expansion"}]}],"id":"blk-66274","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-66277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98367","text":"causal outcome feedback"}]}],"id":"blk-66276","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-66279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-98368","text":"goal tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-66278","kind"